# Dashboard configuration — copy this file to web/.env.local and fill it in.
#
# IMPORTANT: Next.js reads THIS directory's .env.local. It does NOT read the
# .env at the repo root, which is the Python side's. The same Twilio values
# therefore have to appear in both files. That is a Next.js rule, not a choice
# this project made, and it is the reason a correctly-configured .env at the
# root still leaves the dashboard button saying "Preview message".
#
# web/.env.local is git-ignored. Never commit it, and never put these values
# into Vercel — see SETUP.md Part 5. Locally they are fine: the dev server
# listens on your own machine only.

# WhatsApp sending from the dashboard button. Every value masked below; the
# real ones come from your Twilio console.
TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID=AC••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••   # 34 chars, starts AC
TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN=••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••      # 32 chars — a password
TWILIO_WHATSAPP_NUMBER=+1415•••••••                     # shared sandbox number

# The ONLY number the dashboard will send to. The send endpoint ignores any
# recipient in the request and uses this, so the button cannot be pointed at
# anyone else. Your own phone, in +61... form.
WHATSAPP_TO=+614••••••••

# Optional
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=http://localhost:3000
